\n## Evidence\\n- **Migration Change**: `CREATE INDEX (non-concurrent) on orders(customer_id)`\\n- **Postgres Metrics**: `postgres.locks_waiting` spiked to 74; `postgres.connections_used` hit max capacity (100).\\n- **Application Logs**: `ERROR orders-api: canceling statement due to statement timeout (5000ms)`\\n\\n## Remediation\\n1. Terminate the blocking migration/query on PostgreSQL.\\n2. Re-run the index creation using `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` during a maintenance window.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n- Update CI/CD migration linters to forbid non-concurrent index creations on production tables.\\n- Review connection pool timeout settings and alerting thresholds for database lock contention.\"\n}\n```", "output_ref": null, "tool_calls": [], "output_tokens": 701, "latency_ms": 3460, "input_tokens": 20269, "cached": false, "provider": "gemini"}
